  "notes": "{誇張|こちょう} means exaggeration — making something seem greater or more extreme than it actually is. Used as both a noun and a する verb.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {誇張|こちょう}する: to exaggerate\n- {誇張|こちょう}なしに: without exaggeration\n- {誇張|こちょう}が{過|す}ぎる: to exaggerate too much\n- {誇張|こちょう}{表現|ひょうげん}: hyperbole, exaggerated expression\n- {誇張|こちょう}して{言|い}う: to say with exaggeration\n\nLITERARY TERM:\n{誇張法|こちょうほう} is the rhetorical device of hyperbole.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {大|おお}げさ: exaggerated, dramatic (na-adjective, more colloquial)\n- {言|い}い{過|す}ぎ: overstatement, saying too much\n- オーバー: over-the-top (casual loanword usage)\n\nREGISTER:\nSomewhat formal. In casual speech, {大|おお}げさ is more common.",
